Falsifies `line_editor::line_disc::verification::a_range_delete_removes_exactly_its_range`.

The defect: a cursor inside the deleted range keeps its old column instead of moving to the start
of the range, so after the delete it points into bytes that now belong to the tail, or past the
end of the shortened line. Backspace and forward delete never leave the cursor inside the range
(it is at one end), so only a range that spans the cursor shows the defect.

Expected to fail: the harness's check that the cursor lands on `a` when it was inside the range.

